## Chapter 3: MAWIS Architecture — The Six-Layer System

MAWIS is structured as a six-layer Cognitive Hydric State Operating System. Each layer is technically specified, institutionally grounded, and connected to adjacent layers through defined interfaces.

```
Layer 6: MAWIS-0 — Transition & Incentive Control System
Layer 5: NHIC — National Hydric Intelligence Council (Governance)
Layer 4: IDOE — Integrated Desalination Optimization Engine
Layer 3: SAWAS — Smart Agricultural Water Allocation System
Layer 2: PDIE — Predictive Drought Intelligence Engine
Layer 1: AIP — Aquifer Intelligence Platform (Sensing)
```

The architecture follows a strict dependency structure: each upper layer depends on outputs from lower layers. The sensing layer feeds the prediction layer; prediction feeds allocation; allocation feeds infrastructure scheduling; governance provides authority over all layers; and the transition layer manages the migration from current state to full deployment.

