## Chapter 11: Implementation Roadmap

### Phase 1 — Foundation and Shadow Mode (2026–2028)

Deploy AIP sensing networks in Souss-Massa and Haouz — highest stress, largest irrigated area. Launch PDIE seasonal forecasting for Atlantic-facing basins. Deploy SAWAS pilot in the Haouz perimeter (20,000 farmers, 50,000 ha). Begin MAWIS shadow mode — all systems generate recommendations, no enforcement. Establish NHIC legal framework through parliamentary process. Estimated investment: 180 million USD (World Bank and EIB co-financing eligible).

### Phase 2 — Scaling and Incentive Activation (2028–2031)

Expand AIP to all seven priority aquifers. Launch IDOE for Agadir and Casablanca desalination plants. Activate MAWIS-0 Water Pricing Gradient Phase 2 (subsidy restructuring). Expand SAWAS to Souss-Massa, Gharb, and Moulouya perimeters. Publish first three annual National Water Accounts — establishing public baseline. Estimated investment: 320 million USD.

### Phase 3 — Full National Integration (2031–2035)

Full national MAWIS deployment. Constitutional Water Sovereignty Amendment ratification. NHIC operational with full binding authority. MAWIS-0 Phase 3 water pricing enforcement. Morocco as reference architecture for semi-arid water governance. International licensing of MAWIS framework to interested governments. Estimated investment: 150 million USD (largely self-financing through water pricing revenue).

